<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Login | <%= appInfo.name %></title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg: linear-gradient(135deg, #f0e6dd 0%, #e0eef7 100%);
            --panel: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82);
            --border: #d2c3b8;
            --accent: #0c7489;
            --accent-soft: #d9eff3;
            --text: #24313a;
            --muted: #62707a;
            --danger: #8a2b12;
        }

        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        body {
            margin: 0;
            font-family: "Trebuchet MS", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            min-height: 100vh;
            display: grid;
            place-items: center;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        .shell {
            width: min(980px, 100%);
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
            gap: 18px;
        }
        .panel {
            background: var(--panel);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 28px;
            padding: 28px;
            box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
        }
        .pill {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            min-height: 34px;
            padding: 0 12px;
            border-radius: 999px;
            background: var(--accent-soft);
            color: var(--accent);
            font-size: 0.84rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        }
        h1 {
            margin: 12px 0 8px;
        }
        p, li, label {
            color: var(--muted);
            line-height: 1.6;
        }
        form {
            display: grid;
            gap: 14px;
            margin-top: 18px;
        }
        label {
            display: grid;
            gap: 6px;
            font-weight: 700;
        }
        input {
            width: 100%;
            min-height: 48px;
            padding: 0 14px;
            border-radius: 16px;
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            background: white;
            font: inherit;
            color: var(--text);
        }
        button, .link-btn {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            min-height: 46px;
            padding: 0 16px;
            border-radius: 999px;
            border: 1px solid var(--accent);
            background: var(--accent);
            color: white;
            font: inherit;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-decoration: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        .secondary {
            background: transparent;
            color: var(--text);
            border-color: var(--border);
        }
        .actions {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 10px;
            margin-top: 18px;
        }
        .error {
            padding: 14px 16px;
            border-radius: 18px;
            background: #fff0ec;
            border: 1px solid #e7b6a8;
            color: var(--danger);
        }
        .mono {
            font-family: Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
            font-size: 0.94rem;
            word-break: break-word;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="shell">
        <section class="panel">
            <span class="pill">Custom Sign-in Page</span>
            <h1>Keep your own page, keep Cognito SSO</h1>
            <p>This page is rendered by your app. When you continue, the app redirects the browser to Cognito's authorization endpoint. That means Cognito still owns the actual password step and can reuse its existing browser session for SSO.</p>

            <% if (error) { %>
                <div class="error">
                    <strong>Sign-in start failed</strong>
                    <div class="mono"><%= error %></div>
                </div>
            <% } %>

            <form method="post" action="/login">
                <label>
                    Username or email
                    <input type="text" name="username" value="<%= formValues.username %>" autocomplete="username">
                </label>
                <button type="submit">Continue with Cognito</button>
            </form>

            <div class="actions">
                <a class="link-btn secondary" href="/">Back to Home</a>
                <a class="link-btn secondary" href="/public-page">Open Public Page</a>
                <a class="link-btn secondary" href="/login/direct">Skip hint and continue</a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="panel">
            <h2>How this preserves SSO</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Base URL:</strong> <span class="mono"><%= appInfo.baseUrl %></span></li>
                <li><strong>Issuer:</strong> <span class="mono"><%= appInfo.issuer %></span></li>
                <li><strong>Domain:</strong> <span class="mono"><%= appInfo.domain %></span></li>
                <li><strong>App Client ID:</strong> <span class="mono"><%= appInfo.clientId %></span></li>
                <li><strong>Callback URL:</strong> <span class="mono"><%= appInfo.redirectUri %></span></li>
            </ul>
            <p>Your page stays local and branded, but the browser still goes through Cognito Hosted UI for the real sign-in step. That is the key reason SSO stays compatible with <span class="mono">app1</span> and <span class="mono">app2</span>.</p>
        </section>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
